    "updated_at": "2021-01-12T19:42:21Z",
    "body": "> I think this sounds good, but the default format strings aren't very compatible with missing `$version`. Modules wind up with one/two spaces from `$symbol` and one from the end of the format string. Maybe all the symbols should have one space less and the format strings switched to something like: `via [$symbol( $version)]($style) `?\n\nAh, good catch I didn't notice that in my local testing. Maybe we could just change it to `via [$symbol($version )]($style)` that should avoid us having to change the spacing on the symbols which might break for users who have custom symbols.\n\nAlso we should check that the modules that are already lazily evaluating the commands have the correct format strings. ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
